think ALES57 held the gate and ALES58 held the compressor; both named the last of the three: give the limiter (ALES55) the same hold. This rung completes the HELD dynamics trio — limiter, compressor, and gate all reading one proven held follower (hold_env.env_step_hold), the exact mirror of the un-held trio (ALES53-55) all reading one proven plain follower. The lookahead delay stays the Keaton's-word horizon; the held-follower spend is self-approvable.
think The design is the compressor's mirror: limit_env_hold.rye mirrors ALES55's limit_env.rye with the plain follower swapped for the held one and hold_left carried beside env. The gain math is ALES49's (gain ceil/e above the ceiling — the compressor at an infinite ratio, the target pinned to the ceiling), the time base ALES56's; no arithmetic added on the audio path. The crux law is the zero-hold limit: hold_samples == 0 reduces env_step_hold to env_step, so this limiter reduces to ALES55's limit_follow byte-for-byte.
think The hold-specific proof is the compressor's, not the gate's: the limiter's hold keeps the gain reduction ENGAGED across a duck (the held sample attenuated, quieter), so held magnitude <= un-held everywhere, strictly quieter at the duck. Signal [15000, 300, 15000], ceil 1500, instant attack/release, hold 0 vs 1: un-held releases at the duck and passes 300 (the pump); held pins env=15000 and limits 300 to 30 (gain 1500/15000). Same shape as the compressor because both keep the gain DOWN.
think Like the compressor, the limiter's branch is e > ceil >= 1, so the envelope is strictly positive there — no zero-envelope divide to guard. Only the gate's branch (e < threshold, e can reach 0) needed the forced-unit-step guard.
think Monotonic stamp: live clock read 20260814.182307 (TZ=America/New_York), after ALES58's 181719 — later-is-larger holds.
